L["How AME shares with your guild. v2 (the default) sends each scan once to the whole guild, in small numbered pieces: a lost piece is sent again on its own, a /reload doesn't start a transfer over, and hours you missed - up to a week back - are filled in from whoever has them, so the 7D chart has a point for every hour someone scanned. v1 is the original: each player asks for each scan separately, over the last 48 hours. Pick v1 if sync seems to slow your game; v2 players keep sharing with you. Trusted players outside the guild always use v1."] = true
L["How fast the item moves: units that disappeared between consecutive full scans of this auction house, per day, over the last week. Scans can't tell a sale from a listing that expired or was cancelled, so where you or your guildmates have listed the item, only its sell-through's share counts as sold - an item reposted every day that never sells drops to about 0. Elsewhere treat it as a rough upper bound. A cheap item that never sells is a trap; a high number means you can sell a stack quickly. Needs a few full scans on the same day to show."] = true
