L["How many do you need?"] = true
L["How many steadily listed items rose against how many fell over the chosen period. A rising index with weak breadth means a few items are carrying it."] = true
L["How many units at the buy house still pay after the cut, of how many are listed there. The first number needs the item's listings: search it at the buy house (it then stays for 6 hours)."] = true
L["How many units you can buy at the buy auction house before the route stops paying, and the total profit: every listing priced below what one sells for after the cut. It needs the item's listings, so search the item at the buy house first (the Search button does it) - it then stays for 6 hours. Selling that many still takes time: check Sales/day."] = true
L["How much of what was listed actually sold, in units: sold / (sold + expired + cancelled). It comes from real auction outcomes - your auction mail and cancels, and your guildmates' (shared automatically) - and recent ones count most. With a few outcomes it takes over from the scans: the sales rate, what a listing nets (VENDOR, DE) and the value of what you hold (worth the market price when it sells, the vendor's price when it doesn't)."] = true
L["How much the market price moved compared with 7 days of data ago. Green is up, red is down."] = true
L["How much the price jumps from day to day (the spread of daily % changes over 30 days). Low numbers mean a stable, predictable item; high numbers mean risky swings - and bigger opportunities."] = true
L["How much to trust a number"] = true
L["How much to trust the numbers: 3 green bars = plenty of recent scans, 2 amber = some, 1 red = few or old. More scans of the item (full scans or searches) raise it."] = true
L["How old the latest price for this item is. Rows older than 3 days fade: scan again (or let a guildmate's scan arrive) before trusting them."] = true
L["How old the older of the two prices is. Fresh data on both sides makes a route trustworthy - scan both auction houses (alts on this account count) before buying."] = true
L["How prices across the whole auction house moved, as one number: 100 thirty days ago. Each day it moves by the average price change of steadily listed items - listed on most days, at least 3 at a time - so one-off and fantasy listings can't move it. Above 100: things got more expensive."] = true
