L["What all your characters hold, valued at your faction's market, with cost and unrealized profit for what you bought on the AH, the Buy/Hold/Sell signal and how long it would take to sell. The ledger lists your AH sales and purchases - recorded from auction mail when you open your mailbox."] = true
L["What listing one at the sell house costs up front: a share of the item's vendor price (faction AH 5/20/60% for 2/8/24 hours, goblin AH five times that), at least 1 silver. You get it back when it sells and lose it if it doesn't - so a high deposit on a slow seller is real risk."] = true
L["What really sells"] = true
L["What the item typically sells for right now. From full listing data it's the average of the cheapest 15-30% of the supply on the auction house, which ignores a few cheap or absurd listings. From a browse summary (what many scanners do by default) only the cheapest listing is known, so then it's the lowest price."] = true
L["What the path nets under each goal (the one in use is marked)."] = true
L["What to post at so it sells within the listing time - instead of undercutting the cheapest listing by 1c. Buyers take the cheapest listings first, so AME counts the units ahead of you at each price, how fast the item sells, and how often new listings undercut you, and weighs the chance of selling against the deposit you lose if it doesn't. Quick sells within a few hours almost surely, Normal is the best price for the chance, Patient is the highest price that still sells about half the time. It learns every item's pattern from your scans (busy hours, weekdays, how hard sellers compete) and from your own posts: if items keep expiring at its prices it gets more careful for that item. With little data it borrows from similar items; the bars show how much it knows."] = true
L["What you paid per unit for the units you bought on the auction house (oldest purchases are sold first). Items you looted or crafted have no cost."] = true
L["What your characters' professions earn at today's prices: top earners, selling materials raw or refined, and recipes on the auction house worth buying. Open each profession once so AME knows your recipes. Needs the AME Crafting Data addon."] = true
