L["With Crafting on, a recipe's tooltip (pattern, plans, formula...) also shows what it makes at today's market price, and what one craft earns after buying the reagents at market and the auction house's cut - red when it loses money. It prices every reagent at market; the Crafting tab also counts the reagents you hold and those cheaper to craft yourself, so its number can differ."] = true
L["With the Market overview switched on (Settings, General), the toolbar's first buttons switch the Market tab between the Screener (this list) and the Overview: indexes and totals for the whole auction house (see Market overview)."] = true
L["With the auction house open, Shift-click a row to search for it there. While the search box has focus, Shift-click an item link anywhere to search for it by name."] = true
L["With v2 (the default), every scan goes to the whole guild at once, and hours you missed in the last week are filled in from whoever has them - a point per hour for the 7D chart, and whole days for days you have nothing of. It's paced at about one message a second, so a full scan takes several minutes to arrive, in the background. If sync seems to slow your game, pick v1 (lighter) under Guild sharing: you still get scans, the original way. The status under Guild sharing shows how many of the week's hours you have and what's on its way."] = true
L["With your profession window open, adds the reagents of the selected recipe - as many times as you'll craft it."] = true
L["Within its usual range"] = true
L["Without Auctionator, the auction house window gets an AME Shopping tab next to Buy, Sell and Auctions. Pick a list on the left and click Search all: AME searches each item in turn, as fast as the game allows, and shows how many you still need, the cheapest listing, how many are on sale at or under your top price, and what the rest costs. Click an item for its listings; Buy asks the game for the price, then Confirm buys it - the game wants a click for each purchase. The list counts down as you buy."] = true
